#
# prima-materia — New Thought: Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to
# Success (1940)
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:NewThought, kept apart from
# traditions/new-thought.ttl, which declares the tradition and its works
# (pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess is declared there, not here). The whole
# book was read, pp. 148-237, in the order of its fourteen addresses; the
# nodes follow the chapters and, within each, the page that carries them.
# Every source names the chapter title as the contents page gives it.
#
# The text read is not the 1940 print. It is Book Three of the eBook "The
# Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn" (eBook edition copyright 2007,
# www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com), pp. 148-237, whose page numbers stand on
# their own line at the foot of each page. Two archive.org uploads of this
# eBook were read as mutual witnesses: TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn
# for the text and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn, a second OCR of the
# same pages, where the first is garbled (contents "I Shall Never Want",
# p. 208 "Let us"). The DeVorss print of 1940, archive.org
# secretdoortosucc00flor, is access-restricted and was not read, so whether
# the eBook keeps the wording and order of 1940 is unchecked; every source
# says so.
#
# Every record of this harvest was compared with the nodes of
# traditions/new-thought-game-of-life.ttl, traditions/new-thought-your-word-
# is-your-wand.ttl and traditions/new-thought.ttl. Where a node there carries
# the same being, practice, caution or capacity, no node is written here and
# links point at it: pmc:NewThoughtShinnLordReadAsLaw, pmp:NewThoughtShinnActingRich,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSpiritualAttitudeTowardsMoney,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnHisGiftsAreForAllEternity,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnInfiniteIntelligence, pmc:NewThoughtShinnHoarding,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnMagicPurseOfTheSpirit,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnImpressingPresupposesActiveFaith, pmc:NewThoughtShinnSoul,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSubconsciousMind, pmp:NewThoughtShinnGiverAndTheGift,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnNothingIsTooGoodToBeTrue, pmp:NewThoughtShinnLawOfForgiveness,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnFreeFromMistakes, pmc:NewThoughtShinnPersonalWill,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire, pmc:NewThoughtShinnMyShipsComeIn,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnFollowingAHunch, pmc:NewThoughtShinnMyPromisedLand,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnRunsAfterHim, pmc:NewThoughtShinnFallsAwayOfItsOwnWeight,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnImagingFaculty,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnImagingFacultyIsTheCreativeFaculty, pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoodWill,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfGrace, pmp:NewThoughtShinnPerfectWay,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuperconsciousMind, pmp:NewThoughtShinnMakingBelieve,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnPreparesForFailure,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnAWayOutOfEverySituation,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnWorldOfTheWondrous, pmc:NewThoughtShinnSoldToTheRightPerson,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineMind, pmp:NewThoughtShinnReceivedOnTheInvisiblePlane,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineDesign, pmc:NewThoughtShinnWhateverIShouldKnowRevealed,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnLivingInThePast, pmp:NewThoughtShinnLiveFullyInTheNow,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheSupplyPrecedesTheDemand,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnDemandForTheDivineDesign and
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnIFulfillMyDestiny. Links also point at
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeemingImpossibleGoodComesToPass,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfKarma, pmc:NewThoughtShinnFaith and
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnPowerOfTheWord. Where this book states a claim of those
# files differently, the node carries a note beginning "Differs from". No
# node of the Quimby Manuscripts carries a claim of this book.
#
# Harvested under prima-materia#924 with two independent extraction passes
# over the text (A 521 records, B 350; 6 records of B without counterpart in
# A: 3 added to A, 3 covered, 0 not owed), then integrated by a reader of the
# whole text. Identifiers are pmc:NewThoughtShinn or pmp:NewThoughtShinn plus
# the author's own wording in PascalCase. Signs of success, conditions of
# failure and capacities carry a note beginning "Counted as". Cases the
# author tells of clients and others are entered as third-party ascriptions,
# her own as first-person reports.
#


#
# The Secret Door to Success
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMetaphysicalInterpretation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "All Bible stories carry a metaphysical reading"@en, "Alle biblischen Geschichten haben eine metaphysische Deutung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that every biblical narrative has an inner, metaphysical interpretation, which is the hermeneutic used throughout the addresses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 150; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWallOfJericho a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wall of Jericho as self-built barrier to success"@en, "Mauer von Jericho als selbstgebaute Schranke vor dem Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each person is said to have success destined for him behind a wall he himself has erected; the city behind it holds his divinely designed success and heart's desire."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"your wall of Jericho\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 150; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWallOfResentment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resentment shuts off one's good"@en, "Groll sperrt das eigene Gute ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "Resenting a person or a situation is named as a wall that cuts off one's good; resenting the success of another keeps one's own success away."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnSecretDoorOfSuccess fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 150; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEnvyNeutralized a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Neutralizing envy and resentment"@en, "Neutralisierung von Neid und Groll"@de ;
    skos:definition "The statement is said to neutralize envy and resentment and so to stop them from keeping the good away."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhatGodHasDoneForOthersAffirmation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation claiming for oneself, and more, the blessings God gave others"@en, "Affirmation: Was Gott für andere tat, tut er nun für mich und mehr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeat the statement that God now does for oneself what he has done for others, and more; given by the author against envy and resentment. Repeated in Ch. 2 for anyone resentful or envious."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"What God has done for others ... for me and more\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnExactDuplicateOfTheGift a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving a duplicate of an envied gift"@en, "Erhalt eines Duplikats des beneideten Geschenks"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman envious of a friend's present used the statement and received an exact copy of the gift plus an additional present."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnShoutOfTruth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation of Truth as the shout that topples the wall"@en, "Wahrheitsaffirmation als der Ruf, der die Mauer stürzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "As the Israelites' shout brought down Jericho, making an affirmation of Truth is said to make one's own barrier totter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWallOfJerichoTotters a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wall tottering when an affirmation is made"@en, "Mauer wankt beim Aussprechen der Affirmation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: as soon as a Truth affirmation is spoken, the barrier to success begins to shake."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text names it as a mark that the work has taken effect. Counted apart from conditions of failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWallsOfLackAndDelay a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Walls-of-lack-and-delay affirmation"@en, "Affirmation: Die Mauern von Mangel und Verzögerung zerfallen, ich betrete mein Gelobtes Land in Gnade"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declare that the barriers of lack and of delay are now falling and that one is entering one's Promised Land, under grace; the author gives it to all hearers at the close of Ch. 1."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"The walls of lack and delay now crumble away\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnSteppingOverAFallenWall a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Picturing oneself stepping over a fallen wall"@en, "Sich vorstellen, über eine eingestürzte Mauer zu steigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "While using the walls-of-lack statement, hold a vivid inner image of stepping over a wall that has fallen down."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDemonstrationOfHerGood a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Demonstration of one's good (removal of lack and delay)"@en, "Demonstration des eigenen Guten (Aufhebung von Mangel und Verzögerung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A demonstration is the visible arrival of the desired good; here it came nearly at once after the statement and picture."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"demonstration\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRadioActivity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Words and thoughts as radio-activity"@en, "Worte und Gedanken als Radioaktivität"@de ;
    skos:definition "The spoken word of realization is what changes one's affairs, because words and thoughts are held to act like a form of radio-activity."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"radio-activity\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnVibratoryForce (The Game of Life, p. 15): there words and thoughts are a vibration shaping body and circumstances; here they are likened to radio-activity, and change in one's affairs is laid on the realizing word."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnInterestInYourWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking interest in and enjoying one's work"@en, "Interesse an der Arbeit nehmen und sie genießen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Become absorbed in and enjoy what one is doing, dramatize one's situation, and make it interesting to others; be interested oneself so that others find one interesting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSecretDoorOfSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening the secret door of success"@en, "Öffnen der geheimen Tür zum Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gaining one's destined success; the work names several keys to it (interest in work, a smile, silence, courage, the spoken word)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the secret door of success\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 151; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

