pmc:NewThoughtShinnLivingInThePastBuildsAWall a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living in the past and complaining builds a thick wall"@en, "In der Vergangenheit leben und klagen baut eine dicke Mauer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dwelling on the past and voicing one's misfortunes is named as a cause of the barrier to success."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnSecretDoorOfSuccess fails."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnLivingInThePast (The Game of Life, p. 35): there dwelling on bygone days is a method of failure in general; here backward-looking complaint is one of the walls built around one's Jericho."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 152; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnInterestInYourWorkYieldsSecretDoorOfSuccessInACase a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Taking interest in and enjoying one's work yields Opening the secret door of success"@en, "Interesse an der Arbeit nehmen und sie genießen: Öffnen der geheimen Tür zum Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told as a case of a client, student or acquaintance: taking interest in and enjoying one's work was followed by Opening the secret door of success."@en ;
    skos:note "The author met Jim Tully, a former tramp, on a ship; he became a known author by dramatizing tramp life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnInterestInYourWork ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnSecretDoorOfSuccess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 152; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnASmileOpensTheSecretDoorYieldsSecretDoorOfSuccess a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cultivating a good disposition and a smile yields Opening the secret door of success"@en, "Eine gute Gemütsart und ein Lächeln pflegen: Öffnen der geheimen Tür zum Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that cultivating a good disposition and a smile brings about Opening the secret door of success."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnASmileOpensTheSecretDoor ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnSecretDoorOfSuccess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
