pmc:NewThoughtShinnYouAttractWhatYouThinkOf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One attracts what one gives much thought to"@en, "Man zieht an, woran man viel denkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thinking much about a thing draws it; much thought on lack draws lack, much thought on injustice draws more injustice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 1 \"The Secret Door to Success\", p. 155; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnThoughtOfLackAttractsLack a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dwelling on lack or injustice attracts more of it"@en, "Verweilen bei Mangel oder Unrecht zieht mehr davon an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition: habitual thought on lack or injustice is said to bring more of the same."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnSecretDoorOfSuccess fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
