#
# Bricks Without Straw
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBricksWithoutStraw a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Making bricks without straw: accomplishing the seemingly impossible"@en, "Ziegel ohne Stroh: das scheinbar Unmögliche vollbringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working with spiritual law one is said to achieve what seems impossible, since God opens a path where none exists."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"make bricks without straw\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeemingImpossibleGoodComesToPass (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 12): there the good that seemed impossible simply arrives; here it is a task carried out without the means for it, read from Exodus 5."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 158; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHouseOfBondage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bondage in Egypt as bondage to destructive thinking"@en, "Knechtschaft in Ägypten als Knechtschaft unter zerstörerischem Denken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exodus 5 is read as everyday life: Pharaoh and the taskmasters stand for destructive thinking, pride, fear, resentment and ill-will; Moses' deliverance stands for the liberty one wins on learning the law of life. Quoted from Agnes M. Lawson."@en ;
    skos:note "Read through a quotation of Agnes M. Lawson, Hints to Bible Students."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 158; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnUnderGrace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Coming under grace"@en, "Unter die Gnade kommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state in which the law is fulfilled and good comes easily; the frequent phrase under grace in the statements refers to it."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"under grace\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 158; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearOfTheLaw a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of the Lord re-read as fear of Karmic law"@en, "Furcht des Herrn umgedeutet als Furcht vor dem Karmagesetz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author explicitly sets her reading (fear of the law) against the conventional one (fear of God) for Psalm 111."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a dispute: the author rejects the view named; the other side is not read and is entered only as she reports it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnLordReadAsLaw (The Game of Life, p. 40): there reading Lord as law means that the law, not God, takes vengeance; here the reading turns the fear of the Lord in Psalm 111 into fear of one's own boomerangs, against the usual sense."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 158; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnUnderGracePresupposesLawOfKarma a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing the law before coming under grace"@en, "Das Gesetz kennen, bevor man unter die Gnade kommt"@de ;
    skos:definition "One cannot come under grace without first knowing the law, which has to be known before it can be fulfilled (quoted from Lawson)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnUnderGrace ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfKarma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One never comes under grace." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 158; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPharaohsHardenedHeart a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pharaoh's literal hardened heart as boomerang"@en, "Pharaos buchstäblich verhärtetes Herz als Bumerang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing a medical report on the mummy of the oppressing Pharaoh, whose arteries had hardened, the author concludes that the king's inner hardness literally stiffened his own heart."@en ;
    skos:note "Illustration of the come-back law from a medical journal report."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
