pmp:NewThoughtShinnKeptMakingHerAffirmations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Continuing to affirm when no channel is visible"@en, "Weiter affirmieren, wenn kein Kanal sichtbar ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "When every avenue is exhausted, keep making affirmations (here a Truth student needing rent) and follow the lead that appears."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 159; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGodMakesAWayYieldsBricksWithoutStraw a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Way-where-there-is-none affirmation yields making bricks without straw: accomplishing the seemingly impossible"@en, "Affirmation: Gott schafft einen Weg, wo kein Weg ist: Ziegel ohne Stroh: das scheinbar Unmögliche vollbringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that way-where-there-is-none affirmation brings about making bricks without straw: accomplishing the seemingly impossible."@en ;
    skos:note "Ch. 2 first gives the phrase as the meaning of bricks without straw."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnGodMakesAWay ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnBricksWithoutStraw ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
