pmc:NewThoughtShinnSupplyFromNoKnownChannel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Supply through an unexpected channel"@en, "Versorgung durch einen unerwarteten Kanal"@de ;
    skos:definition "The woman's dog pulled her another way and she found a roll of bills exactly covering the rent, owner never found."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 160; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPharaohTheReasoningMind a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pharaoh = the reasoning mind"@en, "Pharao = der verstandesmäßige Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reasoning mind or intellect sits on Pharaoh's throne in consciousness, endlessly saying it cannot be done; also called the army of the aliens."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnArmyOfTheAliens (The Game of Life, p. 18): there the aliens are doubts and fears rising from the subconscious; here the phrase names the reasoning mind, enthroned as Pharaoh, which argues that nothing can be done."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Pharaoh; army of the aliens" ;
    pm:nameRole "the intellect/reasoning mind as inner oppressor that argues against the good" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 160; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnTheUnexpectedHappens a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation that the unexpected occurs and the apparently impossible good arrives"@en, "Affirmation: Das Unerwartete geschieht, mein scheinbar unmögliches Gutes verwirklicht sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Counter the reasoning mind's gloomy suggestions with a lively affirmation that the unexpected occurs and that one's apparently impossible good is now realized."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"The unexpected happens\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 160; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnArgumentOfTheReasoningMindStopped a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Silencing the arguments of the reasoning mind"@en, "Zum Schweigen bringen der Einwände des Verstandes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The statement is said to stop all argument from the reasoning mind, because the idea of the unexpected is one it cannot cope with."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 160; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEnemyThoughts a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Enemies = one's enemy thoughts"@en, "Feinde = die eigenen Feindgedanken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The enemies of the Psalm are one's own doubts, fears and apprehensions."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "enemies" ;
    pm:nameRole "doubts, fears and apprehensions" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
