pmc:NewThoughtShinnLifeFreeFromAllLimitation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from limitation through ideas established in the subconscious"@en, "Freiheit von Begrenzung durch im Unterbewusstsein verankerte Ideen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having the ideas of security, health, happiness and plenty established in the subconscious would mean a life without limitation, the Kingdom where things are added automatically."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 160; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

