pmp:NewThoughtShinnFeelRichAndSuccessful a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling rich and successful"@en, "Sich reich und erfolgreich fühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cultivate the feeling of being rich and successful, carefree and attuned to abundance."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:NewThoughtShinnActingRich (The Game of Life, p. 16): there one behaves as though the money had come; here one only feels rich and successful, and the gift is said to attach itself by vibration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 161; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuddenChequeOrGift a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sudden receipt of a cheque or gift"@en, "Plötzlicher Erhalt eines Schecks oder Geschenks"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling rich is said to bring suddenly a large cheque or beautiful gift; the wealthy carefree Clara won the coveted fan at a party."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 161; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEnvyShortCircuitsYourGood a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Envy and resentment short-circuit one's good"@en, "Neid und Groll schließen das Gute kurz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The resentful guests who hoped Clara would not win illustrate that envy and resentment cut off one's good."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuddenChequeOrGift fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
