pmc:NewThoughtShinnResentmentTrack a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resentment grows a habit-track and repels opportunity"@en, "Groll gräbt eine Gewohnheitsspur und vertreibt Gelegenheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more one resents the more there is to resent; a track forms in the brain, the face sets in habitual resentment, one is avoided and misses daily opportunities."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnLogsOfSuccess fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 163; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnChangeYourExpression a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing one's facial expression to a pleasant one"@en, "Den Gesichtsausdruck ins Freundliche ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drop the grievance and look pleasant; the author told a sour apple seller he would sell where he stood if he smiled."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 2 \"Bricks Without Straw\", p. 163; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSellingApplesWithASmile a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thriving business after a changed expression"@en, "Florierendes Geschäft nach verändertem Ausdruck"@de ;
    skos:definition "The next day the seller's expression had changed and he did a big business with a smile."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
