#
# And Five of Them Were Wise
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfPreparation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "True prayer means preparation (law of preparation)"@en, "Wahres Gebet bedeutet Vorbereitung (Gesetz der Vorbereitung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The parable of the ten virgins, wise and foolish, teaches that only those who prepare for their good, showing active faith, bring the manifestation; called the law of preparation."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of preparation\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 165; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnManifestation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manifestation of what is prayed for"@en, "Manifestation des Erbetenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The prayed-for good appearing in outer life; with realization comes manifestation."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"manifestation\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 165; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnArmchairFaith a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Armchair faith without action"@en, "Lehnstuhlglaube ohne Handlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Faith felt only in the chair, the silence or meditation will never move mountains; only what one does in the arena of life counts, faith without action being dead."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"armchair faith\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnManifestation fails."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnFaithWithoutWorksIsDead (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 76): there it is a rule that prayer is answered through faith shown in action; here it is named as the way a prayer fails, faith felt in meditation and not carried into conduct."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 165; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnActingRichYieldsManifestation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting rich, acting as if already received yields manifestation of what is prayed for"@en, "Reich handeln, als sei es schon empfangen: Manifestation des Erbetenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that acting rich, acting as if already received brings about manifestation of what is prayed for."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnActingRich ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnManifestation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 165; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnDivinelyDesignedTrip a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation of a divinely designed, divinely financed trip plus preparatory purchase"@en, "Affirmation einer göttlich geplanten, göttlich finanzierten Reise plus vorbereitender Kauf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give thanks for one's divinely designed trip, financed by God, under grace and in perfect fashion; and buy something for it (a trunk) that gives the realization of the trip whenever seen."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"divinely designed trip, divinely financed\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:NewThoughtShinnAffirmationForJourney (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 73): there thanks for a planned journey is the whole of it; here the statement is joined to buying a trunk as preparation for a trip not yet paid for."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 166; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnVibrationOfHisTrip a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being put into the vibration of the desired event (inner sensing)"@en, "In die Schwingung des Ersehnten versetzt werden (inneres Wahrnehmen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The student felt his room move like a ship, smelt the docks, and heard with his inner ear gulls and the gangplank; the trunk had attuned him to the trip's vibration."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"inner ear\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 166; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTookTheTrip a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving money for and taking the desired trip"@en, "Geld für die ersehnte Reise erhalten und sie antreten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Soon after, a large sum came and he took the trip, perfect in every detail."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivinelyPlannedJourney (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 73): there the journey runs under right conditions; here the money for it is first lacking and then arrives."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 166; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnConcertPitch a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping tuned to concert pitch; watching one's motives"@en, "Auf Konzertstimmung bleiben; die eigenen Motive überwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In daily life stay tuned up, and examine diligently whether one acts from fear or from faith."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 166; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWindYourselfUpFinancially a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Winding oneself up financially by always acting one's faith"@en, "Sich finanziell aufziehen, indem man stets seinen Glauben lebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "For money problems, keep oneself wound up by continually acting out faith rather than trusting salary or investments."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 166; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

