pmc:NewThoughtShinnNoMoreThanWasInTheirConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One receives only what is in one's consciousness"@en, "Man empfängt nur, was im eigenen Bewusstsein ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "No one can receive more than is in his consciousness, or what he vibrates to; the wise could not give their oil. With realization comes manifestation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 168; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPreparationWorksBothWays a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Preparation cuts both ways"@en, "Das Gesetz der Vorbereitung wirkt in beide Richtungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Preparing for what one fears attracts it: saving for illness is deliberately preparing to be ill, saving for a rainy day ensures one."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfPreparation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 168; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPreparingForWhatYouFear a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Preparing for what one fears or does not want"@en, "Sich auf das Gefürchtete oder Unerwünschte vorbereiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition: precautionary preparation for misfortune draws the misfortune at an inconvenient time."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnManifestation fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
