pmc:NewThoughtShinnJudgmentDayInSevens a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Judgment day as Karmic payment that comes in sevens"@en, "Jüngster Tag als karmische Zahlung, die in Siebenern kommt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Judgment day is the law of Karma; it is said (they say) to come in sevens: hours, days, weeks, months, years, even minutes; then a karmic debt is paid for violating spiritual law."@en ;
    skos:note "Kept as hearsay: the author marks the reckoning in sevens as what is said."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 169; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnKarmicDebtForNoOil a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paying karmic debt for failing to trust God"@en, "Karmische Schuld für mangelndes Gottvertrauen zahlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failing to trust God and to bring oil for one's lamp brings the price for violating spiritual law, as with the foolish virgins shut out."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnFruitsOfOurFaith fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 169; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnExamineYourConsciousness a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Daily examination of what one is preparing for"@en, "Tägliche Prüfung, worauf man sich vorbereitet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every day examine one's consciousness to see what one is preparing for; use what one has wisely rather than hoarding."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 3 \"And Five of Them Were Wise\", p. 169; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBankOfTheImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing on the imagination as a bank"@en, "Schöpfen aus der Bank der Vorstellungskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The magic-purse statement is said to bring a vivid picture so that one draws on the imagination as on a bank."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the bank of the imagination\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
