#
# What Do You Expect?
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFaithIsExpectancy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Faith is expectancy; one receives according to expectation"@en, "Glaube ist Erwartung; man empfängt gemäß der Erwartung"@de ;
    skos:definition "According to one's faith, read as according to one's expectancies; those who expect the worst invite it, those expecting improvement invite it."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of expectancy\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfExpectancy (The Game of Life, p. 71): there a good message once received is to be harboured until it appears; here faith itself is defined as expectancy, so that whatever is expected, good or bad, comes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnExpectingTheWorst a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Expecting the worst invites it"@en, "Das Schlimmste erwarten lädt es ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Saying one expects the worst or that the worst is still to come deliberately invites it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnChangeYourConditions fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnChangeYourConditions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing one's conditions"@en, "Die eigenen Umstände verändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Changed expectancies are said to change outer conditions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnChangeYourExpectancies a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing one's expectancies by acting as if success were expected"@en, "Die Erwartungen ändern, indem man handelt, als erwarte man Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "To break a habit of expecting loss, behave as though expecting success, happiness and abundance; do something visible that shows one expects the good."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnImpressTheSubconscious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Impressing the subconscious"@en, "Das Unterbewusstsein beeindrucken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Active faith, and it alone, is said to make an impression on the subconscious mind; Ch. 5 adds that a symbol's picture also impresses it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnPrepareForAHome a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Preparing for a home immediately after speaking the word"@en, "Nach dem Sprechen des Wortes sofort ein Heim vorbereiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "After speaking the word for a house, prepare at once as if there were no time to lose, collecting small ornaments and table-cloths."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnGiantSwingIntoFaith a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Symbolic purchase as a giant leap into faith"@en, "Durch einen symbolischen Kauf den großen Sprung in den Glauben wagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Buy an object that presupposes the desired good, e.g. a large armchair for the expected right man."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the giant swing into faith\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheRightManCame a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Arrival of the right partner"@en, "Ankunft des richtigen Partners"@de ;
    skos:definition "The woman who bought a large armchair for the right man is reported to have met him."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 171; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

