pmp:NewThoughtShinnMakeFriendsWithTheThingsYouDesire a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Linking in thought with desired things in shops"@en, "Sich in Gedanken mit ersehnten Dingen in Läden verbinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without money, look in shop windows, enter the shops anyway, try things on, and make friends with what one desires or needs, getting into their vibration."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"make friends with the things you desire\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 172; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRealizationOfOwnership a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Realization of ownership and receipt of the desired object"@en, "Erleben des Besitzes und Erhalt des ersehnten Gegenstands"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman tried on rings and gained such a sense of ownership that soon a friend gave her a ring."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 172; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnNoticingBeautifulThings a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping on noticing beautiful things"@en, "Weiter schöne Dinge bemerken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habitually notice beautiful things to make an invisible contact with them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 172; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnInvisibleContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invisible contact drawing things into one's life"@en, "Unsichtbarer Kontakt, der Dinge ins Leben zieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Noticing beautiful things is said to form an invisible contact so that sooner or later they enter one's life."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 172; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTooGoodToBeTrue a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-pity: calling it too good to be real"@en, "Sagen, es sei zu schön, um wahr zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The noticed things are drawn in unless one says, pitying oneself, that it is too good to be real."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnInvisibleContact fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 172; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnMyExpectationIsFromHim a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling the subconscious to expect everything from God, not channels"@en, "Dem Unterbewusstsein sagen, alles von Gott zu erwarten, nicht von Kanälen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like the psalmist, instruct one's subconscious to expect directly from the universal and not to depend on particular doors or channels."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 172; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDoNotLimitTheChannels a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not limit the channels"@en, "Die Kanäle nicht begrenzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any seemingly impossible good may be expected from God provided the channels are not restricted; neither dictate the manner nor declare it impossible."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnBricksWithoutStraw ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
