pmc:NewThoughtShinnMiracleMinded a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The age is becoming Miracle Minded"@en, "Das Zeitalter wird wundergesinnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are said to be waking to what their words and thoughts can do; the author cites a newspaper piece on the success of metaphysical plays as corroboration."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"Miracle Minded\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 173; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGiverAndTheGiftYieldsMasterOfAllConditions a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thanking God as both Giver and Gift yields mastery of all conditions"@en, "Gott dem Geber für Gott die Gabe danken: Herrschaft über alle Umstände"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that thanking God as both Giver and Gift brings about mastery of all conditions."@en ;
    skos:note "The Giver statement and the seeing-God practice are given together as the means to mastery."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnGiverAndTheGift ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnMasterOfAllConditions ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 173; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeeGodInEveryFaceYieldsMasterOfAllConditions a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing God in every person and good in all situations yields mastery of all conditions"@en, "Gott in jedem Gesicht und das Gute in jeder Lage sehen: Herrschaft über alle Umstände"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that seeing God in every person and good in all situations brings about mastery of all conditions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnSeeGodInEveryFace ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnMasterOfAllConditions ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 173; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGodIsYourLandlordYieldsHeatTurnedOnWithoutAsking a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Realizing that God is one's landlord yields situation resolved without asking"@en, "Erkennen, dass Gott der eigene Vermieter ist: Lösung der Lage ohne Bitte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told as a case of a client, student or acquaintance: realizing that God is one's landlord was followed by situation resolved without asking."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnGodIsYourLandlord ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnHeatTurnedOnWithoutAsking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 173; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnExpectancyThroughSuperstition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The law of expectancy working through superstition"@en, "Das Gesetz der Erwartung wirkt durch Aberglauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Walking under a ladder brings bad luck only because one expects it; expectancy is the substance of things hoped for or feared."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnPsychologyOfSuperstitions (The Game of Life, p. 22): there a lucky charm works by the expectancy it creates; here an omen of bad luck works the same way, and the ladder itself is innocent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 174; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBadLuckBecauseYouExpectedIt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Expecting bad luck from an omen"@en, "Unglück von einem Omen erwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bad luck comes because it was expected, not from the omen itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnChangeYourConditions fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 175; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnExpectTheBlessingsNow a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Expecting far-off blessings now, under grace, unexpectedly"@en, "Ferne Segnungen jetzt erwarten, in Gnade, auf unerwartete Weise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Think of the blessings that seem far off and start expecting them now; extend this to the Bible's promises (said to number three thousand)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 175; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnThreeThousandPromises a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Riches and honor, eternal youth, eternal life"@en, "Reichtum und Ehre, ewige Jugend, ewiges Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Among the Bible's promises to be expected; the author states we now know all these things to be scientifically possible."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnEternalYouth (The Game of Life, p. 47): there the overcoming of death is reached through the subconscious; here eternal youth and life stand with riches and honour among the Bible's promises, to be expected now."@en ;
    skos:note "Strong claim: declared scientifically possible."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 175; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyElectricExpressed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The body electric: body bathed in light, incorruptible"@en, "Der elektrische Leib: lichtdurchfluteter, unvergänglicher Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following forgiveness, bodies are said to be flooded with light and to express an incorruptible, indestructible body of pure substance expressing perfection."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"body electric\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyElectric (The Game of Life, p. 47): there the body is transformed by impressing the subconscious with eternal youth; here it follows release from mistakes under the law of forgiveness and, in Ch. 8, the single eye."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 175; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 8 \"The Watchman at the Gate\", p. 200; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnIExpectTheUnexpected a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Closing affirmation of expecting the unexpected"@en, "Schlussaffirmation: Ich erwarte das Unerwartete, mein herrliches Gutes verwirklicht sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "State that one awaits the unexpected and that one's glorious good is now being realized."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"I expect the unexpected\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 4 \"What Do You Expect?\", p. 175; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnExpectTheBlessingsNowYieldsThreeThousandPromises a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Expecting far-off blessings now, under grace, unexpectedly yields riches and honor, eternal youth, eternal life"@en, "Ferne Segnungen jetzt erwarten, in Gnade, auf unerwartete Weise: Reichtum und Ehre, ewige Jugend, ewiges Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that expecting far-off blessings now, under grace, unexpectedly brings about riches and honor, eternal youth, eternal life."@en ;
