#
# The Long Arm of God
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnArmOfGod a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The arm of God"@en, "Der Arm Gottes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Throughout the Bible God's arm stands for protection and strength; the everlasting arms thrust out the inner enemy thoughts and destroy them; the long arm reaches over people and conditions."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "arm of God; everlasting arms; long arm of God" ;
    pm:nameRole "protective, controlling divine power" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 176; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPowerOfASymbol a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Biblical symbols impress the subconscious"@en, "Biblische Symbole prägen das Unterbewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Bible's writers knew the power of symbols (rock, sheep, shepherd, vineyard, lamp): a symbol brings a picture that impresses the subconscious mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 176; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEnemyBeforeThee a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The enemy before thee = negative thought-forms"@en, "Der Feind vor dir = negative Gedankenformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The enemy is the negative thought-forms one has built in the subconscious; a man's foes are those of his own household."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the enemy before thee" ;
    pm:nameRole "negative thought-forms in the subconscious" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 176; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNegativeThoughtForms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought-forms built up in the subconscious"@en, "Im Unterbewusstsein aufgebaute Gedankenformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeated emotions such as resentment build up thought-forms in the subconscious that keep one boiling and that can be removed with relief."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"thought-form\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 176; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnResentWithEveryOrgan a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Resentment damages every organ of the body"@en, "Groll schädigt jedes Organ des Körpers"@de ;
    skos:definition "One resents with every organ; the penalty is rheumatism, arthritis, neuritis and the like, as acid thoughts are said to produce acid in the blood; it comes from fighting the battle oneself instead of leaving it to God."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnWallOfResentment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 176; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLongArmOfGodYieldsImpressTheSubconscious a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Long-arm-of-God affirmation yields impressing the subconscious"@en, "Affirmation vom langen Arm Gottes: Das Unterbewusstsein beeindrucken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that long-arm-of-God affirmation brings about impressing the subconscious."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnLongArmOfGod ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnImpressTheSubconscious ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 176; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnLongArmOfGod a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Long-arm-of-God affirmation"@en, "Affirmation vom langen Arm Gottes"@de ;
    skos:definition "State that God's long arm extends over people and conditions, governing the situation and guarding one's interests; hold the picture of a long strong arm; given by the author to many students."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"The long arm of God\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 177; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRelaxAndLetGo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing to resist or resent; relaxing and letting go"@en, "Aufhören zu widerstehen oder zu grollen; entspannen und loslassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With the realization of the long arm one no longer resists or resents; enemy thoughts are destroyed and therefore adverse conditions disappear."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 177; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnStandAside a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spiritual development: standing still while Infinite Intelligence fights one's battles"@en, "Geistige Entwicklung: stillstehen, während die Unendliche Intelligenz kämpft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spiritual development is defined as being able to stand still or step aside while Infinite Intelligence lifts burdens and fights battles."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"stand still, or stand aside\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnStandStill (The Game of Life, p. 43): there standing still is named as the hardest thing; here the ability to stand aside is what spiritual development is said to consist in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 177; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSenseOfRelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sense of relief, kindly feeling, organs functioning"@en, "Gefühl der Erleichterung, Wohlwollen, funktionierende Organe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: when the burden of resentment lifts one feels relieved, feels kindly toward all, and the bodily organs start working properly."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text names it as a mark that the work has taken effect. Counted apart from conditions of failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 5 \"The Long Arm of God\", p. 177; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWrongEmotionsCauseIllness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Negative emotions as causes of illness (A. E. Day)"@en, "Negative Gefühle als Krankheitsursachen (A. E. Day)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A quoted clipping by Albert Edward Day holds that poisonous emotions destroy physical health, that loving enemies is a law of hygiene, and that hatred acts like repeated poison. The author adds that without a balanced mind food cannot be digested."@en ;
    skos:note "Quoted from a clipping of Albert Edward Day, D.D."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
