#
# The Fork in the Road
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnForkInTheRoad a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Daily necessity of choice: the fork in the road"@en, "Tägliche Notwendigkeit der Wahl: die Weggabelung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every day brings a fork; the choice is between intellect and divine guidance, fear and faith."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 6 \"The Fork in the Road\", p. 182; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnOtherPeopleMakeDecisions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting others decide, or reasoning things out like a grocer"@en, "Andere entscheiden lassen oder wie ein Krämer abwägen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who rush about letting others decide regret it; those who weigh and measure by reasoning are surprised to miss their goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnMagicPathOfIntuition fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 6 \"The Fork in the Road\", p. 182; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMagicPathOfIntuition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intuition: the magic path"@en, "Intuition: der magische Pfad"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intuition is a spiritual faculty far above the reasoning mind; on its path lies all one desires, and followers reach their Promised Land in a twinkling. Dormant in most people."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the magic path of intuition\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 6 \"The Fork in the Road\", p. 182; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIntuitionIsGodTelephoning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prayer is telephoning to God; intuition is God telephoning you"@en, "Gebet ist Anrufen Gottes; Intuition ist Gottes Anruf bei dir"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoted from the author's correspondence course, framing prayer and intuition as two directions of one line."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
