#
# Crossing Your Red Sea
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMyPromisedLandPresupposesWildernessOrDesert a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Wilderness before the Promised Land"@en, "Eine Wüste vor dem Gelobten Land"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is a wilderness to cross before one's Promised Land is reached, with old doubts and fears encamped around."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnMyPromisedLand ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnWildernessOrDesert ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 7 \"Crossing Your Red Sea\", p. 189; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMosesOnYourPathway a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Moses = whoever tells you to go forward"@en, "Mose = wer dir sagt, vorwärtszugehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A Moses always appears on one's path, sometimes a friend, sometimes intuition; Moses is also portrayed as meek toward the Lord and thereby strong."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Moses" ;
    pm:nameRole "a friend or intuition urging one forward" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 7 \"Crossing Your Red Sea\", p. 190; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBibleTalksAboutTheIndividual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Bible speaks of the individual: your wilderness, Red Sea, Promised Land"@en, "Die Bibel spricht vom Einzelnen: deine Wüste, dein Rotes Meer, dein Gelobtes Land"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Exodus narrative is read as the inner journey of each hearer; the Promised Land is one's heart's desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 7 \"Crossing Your Red Sea\", p. 190; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnReasoningMindBacksTheEgyptians a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The reasoning mind backs up the Egyptians"@en, "Der Verstand unterstützt die Ägypter"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reasoning mind always sides with the negative thoughts and doubts that the Promised Land exists."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "reasoning mind" ;
    pm:nameRole "ally of negative thoughts" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
