pmp:NewThoughtShinnStopHatingThatMan a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing to hate and forgiving the wrongdoer"@en, "Aufhören zu hassen und dem Übeltäter vergeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop hating the person who wronged one, keep attending meetings, and work until forgiveness is complete; the author called it taking one's initiation in forgiveness."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"initiation in forgiveness\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 7 \"Crossing Your Red Sea\", p. 192; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnInitiationInForgiveness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation in forgiveness"@en, "Einweihung in die Vergebung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A trial stage of complete forgiveness, after which one is no longer disturbed and greets the wrongdoer cordially."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"initiation in forgiveness\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
