pmc:NewThoughtShinnMeekAsMoses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Meekness toward divine commands as the source of strength"@en, "Sanftmut gegenüber göttlichem Gebot als Quelle der Stärke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moses is read as the model of self-abnegation: by yielding wholly to the commands of the Lord he became among the strongest men of all and dared to lead the people into the sea."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"As meek as Moses\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Interpreted biblical figure (Exodus 14)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 7 \"Crossing Your Red Sea\", p. 193; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoForward a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling oneself: go forward"@en, "Sich selbst sagen: Geh vorwärts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Think of one's problem and, as Moses did without doubting, say to oneself to go forward."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
