pmc:NewThoughtShinnSingleEye a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The single eye"@en, "Das einfältige (einzige) Auge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having the single eye, one perceives only Truth, sees through evil knowing good comes from it, transmutes injustice into justice; every thought becomes constructive and each word powerful; one is a giant."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"single eye\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnSingleEyeOfTheSpirit (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 81): there a vision of finished good only; here the single eye is placed in the forehead as the seat of imagination and is said to make every thought constructive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 8 \"The Watchman at the Gate\", p. 200; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeemingEnemyDisarmed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disarming a seeming enemy"@en, "Einen scheinbaren Feind entwaffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The goodwill sent is said to disarm the enemy and turn injustice into justice."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 8 \"The Watchman at the Gate\", p. 200; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCyclops a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Cyclops myth arose from the forehead seat of imagination"@en, "Der Kyklopen-Mythos entstand aus dem Stirnsitz der Vorstellung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The one-eyed giants of Sicily are explained as a figure of the imaging faculty seated between the eyes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
