#
# The Way of Abundance
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnOneWayStreet a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Abundance as a one-way street"@en, "Der Weg der Fülle ist eine Einbahnstraße"@de ;
    skos:definition "One heads either to lack or to abundance; rich and poor consciousness walk different mental streets. A lavish supply is divinely planned for each; rich thoughts make rich surroundings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 203; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCrystallizedWords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Your world is crystallized ideas and words; words return spirally"@en, "Deine Welt sind kristallisierte Ideen und Worte; Worte kehren spiralförmig zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Changing thoughts changes conditions in a twinkling; a quotation holds words to be forces moving spirally and returning to their makers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 203; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBemoaningYourLot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Talking lack and bemoaning one's lot"@en, "Von Mangel reden und sein Los beklagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who always talk lack reap it; lamenting one's lot bars entry to the Kingdom of Abundance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnWayOfAbundance fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 203; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIDontWantAnythingICantAfford a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Limited prosperity ideas: making do and wanting nothing one cannot afford"@en, "Begrenzte Wohlstandsideen: sich behelfen und nichts wollen, was man sich nicht leisten kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman who always made old clothes do and repeated she wanted nothing she could not afford had little; her husband left her, tired of her nagging and narrow thinking."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnWayOfAbundance fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 203; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnProveTheLawOfAbundance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Proving the law of abundance"@en, "Das Gesetz der Fülle beweisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use what money one has fearlessly to show faith in invisible supply, rely on God as source, stop voicing lack, keep feeling and looking prosperous, dig one's ditches and give thanks without wavering."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"dug her ditches\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:NewThoughtShinnDiggingDitches (The Game of Life, p. 17): there ditches are dug as preparation for one thing asked for; here a whole way of living is changed to prove the law, with fearless spending, no talk of lack and a prosperous look."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 204; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWayOfAbundance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Swinging into the way of abundance"@en, "In den Weg der Fülle einschwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The woman had more money than ever, unheard-of doors opened, she succeeded in work she had not trained for and stood on miracle ground; many demonstrations came at the eleventh hour but always came."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"miracle ground; eleventh hour demonstrations\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 204; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnPraiseAndThanksgiving a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeking with praise and thanksgiving instead of desperately"@en, "Mit Lob und Dank suchen statt verzweifelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Look for a position not desperately but with praise and thanksgiving, as Jesus, called the greatest metaphysician, taught."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 204; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPraiseOpensTheGates a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening the gates (expectancy wins)"@en, "Öffnen der Tore (Erwartung siegt)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Praise and thanksgiving are said to open the gates because expectancy always wins."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 9 \"The Way of Abundance\", p. 204; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnProveTheLawOfAbundanceYieldsWayOfAbundance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Proving the law of abundance yields swinging into the way of abundance"@en, "Das Gesetz der Fülle beweisen: In den Weg der Fülle einschwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told as a case of a client, student or acquaintance: proving the law of abundance was followed by swinging into the way of abundance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnProveTheLawOfAbundance ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnWayOfAbundance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
