#
# I Shall Never Want
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAbundanceOfTheSpheres a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Never wanting: every need met, drawing at once from the spheres' abundance"@en, "Nie Mangel leiden: jedes Bedürfnis gedeckt, sofortiges Schöpfen aus der Fülle der Sphären"@de ;
    skos:definition "With the conviction that the Lord is one's shepherd, every need is said to be met now and forever and one draws at once whatever one needs, since it is already on one's path."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the abundance of the spheres\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 210; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnTheLordIsMyShepherd a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shepherd affirmation (Psalm 23)"@en, "Affirmation: Der Herr ist mein Hirte, mir wird nichts mangeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take the Psalm statement until one has the conviction that the Lord, Infinite Intelligence, supplies every need; it closes Ch. 10."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"The Lord is my Shepherd, I shall never want\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
