pmc:NewThoughtShinnInvisibleSupply a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Touching one's invisible supply; feeling outside time and space"@en, "Den unsichtbaren Vorrat berühren; sich außerhalb von Zeit und Raum fühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman with the sudden realization felt herself touching her invisible supply, outside time and space, no longer relying on the outer; then found needed paperclips in an unused chest, and money and other things followed."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"invisible supply\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 210; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAskingGodForMoney a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the view that asking God for money or things is wrong"@en, "Gegen die Ansicht, es sei falsch, Gott um Geld oder Dinge zu bitten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author rejects the pious opinion she used to hear, saying its holders did not know the Creative Principle dwells in everyone and that real spirituality means proving God as supply daily."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a dispute: the author rejects the view named; the other side is not read and is entered only as she reports it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 210; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAbundanceOfTheSpheresPresupposesTheLordIsMyShepherd a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Conviction that the Lord is shepherd before never wanting"@en, "Überzeugung, dass der Herr der Hirte ist, vor dem Nie-Mangeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is never in want once one holds the realization or conviction; gaining it today meets every need."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnAbundanceOfTheSpheres ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnTheLordIsMyShepherd ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
