pmc:NewThoughtShinnCreativePrinciple a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Creative Principle (within each man)"@en, "Das Schöpferische Prinzip (in jedem Menschen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A principle within each person, one with him (paraphrasing Jesus on oneness with the Father); Pure Intelligence that knows the way of fulfillment and must be fully trusted."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Creative Principle; great Creative Principle of the Universe; Pure Intelligence" ;
    pm:nameRole "indwelling creative divine principle identical with man" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 211; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTrueSpirituality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "True spirituality as daily proof of God as supply"@en, "Wahre Spiritualität heißt, Gott täglich als Versorgung zu beweisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not occasionally but every day; with this realization hoarding and saving vanish, and a loss in one direction brings a gain in another."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 211; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGreatestOfMetaphysicians a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus Christ as the greatest metaphysician who knew the law"@en, "Jesus Christus als größter Metaphysiker, der das Gesetz kannte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Jesus is held to have known the supply law, so whatever he required appeared at once on his path (loaves, fishes, coin from the fish); called the greatest of metaphysicians; his mission was to wake people to one power."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Jesus Christ" ;
    pm:nameRole "master metaphysician and exemplar of the law" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 211; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnStatementWhichClicksForSupply a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Contacting invisible supply by a statement that clicks"@en, "Kontakt zum unsichtbaren Vorrat durch eine einrastende Aussage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make contact with one's invisible supply by a statement of Truth that clicks and gives realization; open to all, not a chosen few."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
