pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessBuiltUponAFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Big successes built on failures"@en, "Fast jeder große Erfolg ist auf einem Misserfolg gebaut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illustrated by Edgar Bergen, who lost a Broadway part and then became famous on radio."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnApparentFailure (The Game of Life, p. 19): there seeming failure comes just before a great accomplishment; here most big successes are said to rest on an actual failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 212; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDarknessBeforeTheDawn a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not be deceived by the dark before dawn"@en, "Lass dich nicht von der Dunkelheit vor der Dämmerung täuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author told of a poor discouraged man who ended his life days before learning of a large inheritance; a hearer quipped that wanting to be dead means the demonstration is three days off."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnDarkestBeforeTheDawn (The Game of Life, p. 18): there the dark hour is announced as the stirring of old beliefs by a high statement; here it is a warning, after a story of a suicide days before an inheritance, not to be fooled by it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnDawnOfSuccess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 212; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDawnOfSuccess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The certain dawn of success, joy and abundance"@en, "Die sichere Morgendämmerung von Erfolg, Glück und Fülle"@de ;
    skos:definition "After darkness a dawn comes to each, as unfailing as the sunrise the author watched in Prospect Park after following a hunch."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 214; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnSeekingTheLord a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeking the Lord: making affirmations, expecting and preparing"@en, "Den Herrn suchen: affirmieren, erwarten und vorbereiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Man has to take the first step; seeking the Lord is done by affirmations and by expecting and preparing for the good."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 10 \"I Shall Never Want\", p. 214; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnSpeakTheWord a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment: practitioner speaking the word for a client"@en, "Behandlung: der Praktiker spricht das Wort für einen Klienten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practitioner speaks the word for a specific result (debts wiped out, a sale at the right price, rightness and justice); the client is to hold faith in it."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"treatment; speak the word\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:NewThoughtShinnSpeakingTheWord (The Game of Life, p. 15): there thanks are given in advance for one needed sum; here speaking the word is the practitioner's general treatment for a client, for justice, a sale or a debt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
