#
# Look With Wonder
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBackInTheWorldOfTheWondrousPresupposesILookWithWonder a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A state of consciousness to reach the World of the Wondrous"@en, "Ein Bewusstseinszustand, um die Welt des Wunderbaren zu erreichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only a state of consciousness gives access: becoming as a little child, in joy and wonder."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnBackInTheWorldOfTheWondrous ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnILookWithWonder ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 217; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnILookWithWonder a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Look-with-wonder affirmation"@en, "Affirmation: Ich schaue mit Staunen auf das, was vor mir liegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take the statement, e.g. early in the morning, and look at what comes with childlike wonder; mentioned in the author's first book; closes Ch. 11."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"I look with wonder at that which is before me\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:NewThoughtShinnMessageForTheDay (The Game of Life, p. 37): there the sentence is met in a book and repeated as the day's message, and a sum arrives; here the author takes it the morning after missing an opportunity, and the same offer returns at noon."@en ;
    skos:note "The author says the statement was given her years before and that she cites it in The Game of Life; no speaker is named and the wording is not claimed to come from another speaker, so no pm:Receiving is entered."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 218; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnOpportunityCameAgain a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Return of a missed opportunity"@en, "Rückkehr einer verpassten Gelegenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "After missing a chance the author took the statement in the morning; at noon the phone rang with the same proposition and she took it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 218; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHappyExpectancy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Consciousness filled with happy expectancy"@en, "Von glücklicher Erwartung erfülltes Bewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The statement is said to fill the consciousness with happy expectancy; a friend reported wonderful results."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 218; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGloomyIdeas a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gloomy ideas instilled in childhood"@en, "In der Kindheit eingeprägte düstere Ideen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sayings like do not expect too much or you cannot have everything, and unhappy experiences, drive children out of the wondrous world; the author at six looked on life with fear and suspicion and now feels younger than then."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnBackInTheWorldOfTheWondrous fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 218; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

