pmc:NewThoughtShinnStatementOfTruthFlashes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A statement of Truth flashing into consciousness and confidence returning"@en, "Eine Wahrheitsaussage blitzt ins Bewusstsein und Zuversicht kehrt zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Read from Psalm 77: the troubled Truth student, assailed by doubt, finds a statement suddenly flashing into mind, remembers past difficulties overcome, and confidence in God returns."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text names it as a mark that the work has taken effect. Counted apart from conditions of failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 221; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhatGodHasDoneBefore a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation that God repeats past blessings, and more"@en, "Affirmation: Was Gott zuvor getan hat, tut er nun für mich und mehr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Summary of Psalm 77; to be said when thinking of past success, happiness or wealth."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"What God has done before, he now does for me\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 221; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnVainImaginings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "All loss comes from one's own vain imaginings"@en, "Aller Verlust kommt aus den eigenen eitlen Vorstellungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear of loss entering consciousness, carrying burdens, fighting battles and reasoning instead of keeping to intuition are named as the origin of loss; in Ch. 13 appearances of evil also come from vain imaginings."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnAllRestored fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 221; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAllRestored a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everything restored in an instant"@en, "Alles im Augenblick wiederhergestellt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Losses from vain imaginings are said to be restored at once, since what Allah gave cannot shrink; also the years the locusts have eaten."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 222; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIronDogging a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not live in one's past childhood (iron dogging)"@en, "Nicht in der vergangenen Kindheit leben (iron dogging)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep the child's wonder but not nostalgia; those who dwell on happy childhood miss the wonderful now; anecdotes of a disillusioning old house with an iron dog and a romance revisited."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"iron dogging\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnLivingInThePast (The Game of Life, p. 35): there dwelling on the past is a method of failure in general; here the warning is against living in one's childhood, under the family word iron dogging, while a child's wonder is still to be kept."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnLivingInThePast ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 11 \"Look With Wonder\", p. 222; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWhatGodHasDoneBeforeYieldsAllRestored a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation that God repeats past blessings, and more yields everything restored in an instant"@en, "Affirmation: Was Gott zuvor getan hat, tut er nun für mich und mehr: Alles im Augenblick wiederhergestellt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that affirmation that God repeats past blessings, and more brings about everything restored in an instant."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhatGodHasDoneBefore ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnAllRestored ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
