#
# Catch Up with Your Good
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnYourGoodPrecedesYou a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Catching up with one's good: it precedes you"@en, "Das eigene Gute einholen: es geht dir voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Answered before calling: the good arrives ahead of one; one must catch up with it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 12 \"Catch Up with Your Good\", p. 224; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAsleepToTheirOpportunities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being asleep to opportunities or lazy"@en, "Für Gelegenheiten schlafen oder träge sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who say no luck ever comes have slept through opportunities or through laziness failed to catch up; a woman refused work to lie abed reading fashion magazines; laziness dulls desire and defies the divine design."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnCatchUpWithYourGood fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 12 \"Catch Up with Your Good\", p. 224; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLazyStatesOfMind a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Avoid slipping into mental laziness"@en, "Nicht in träge Geisteszustände verfallen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explicit warning drawn from the magazine-reading woman."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnCatchUpWithYourGood ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 12 \"Catch Up with Your Good\", p. 224; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWideAwakeToMyGood a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Wide-awake affirmation (never missing a trick)"@en, "Affirmation: Ich bin hellwach für mein Gutes, mir entgeht nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeat the statement; Ch. 14 prescribes it repeatedly to reverse thoughts like my good always comes too late."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"I am wide awake to my good\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:NewThoughtShinnDontLetMeMissATrick (The Game of Life, p. 36): there a silent request not to miss a lead; here a declaration of being already wide awake to one's good, set against laziness and against the belief that good comes too late."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 12 \"Catch Up with Your Good\", p. 224; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNotFollowingHunches a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not following one's hunches"@en, "Den eigenen Ahnungen nicht folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A student says that whenever she fails to follow hunches she gets into a jam."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnCatchUpWithYourGood fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 12 \"Catch Up with Your Good\", p. 224; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCatchUpWithYourGoodPresupposesWakeUpToYourLeads a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Hearing ears and seeing eyes, or the good escapes"@en, "Ohren, die hören, und Augen, die sehen, sonst entgeht das Gute"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hearing ears and seeing eyes are needed to catch up with the good."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnCatchUpWithYourGood ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnWakeUpToYourLeads ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The good escapes one." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 12 \"Catch Up with Your Good\", p. 224; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWideAwakeToMyGoodYieldsCatchUpWithYourGood a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Wide-awake affirmation (never missing a trick) yields catching up with one's good"@en, "Affirmation: Ich bin hellwach für mein Gutes, mir entgeht nichts: Das eigene Gute einholen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that wide-awake affirmation (never missing a trick) brings about catching up with one's good."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnWideAwakeToMyGood ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnCatchUpWithYourGood ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
