pmp:NewThoughtShinnLawOfAgreement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Law of agreement: enlisting a healer, practitioner or friend"@en, "Gesetz der Übereinstimmung: einen Heiler, Praktiker oder Freund hinzuziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Where two agree it shall be done: since one can hardly see one's own good clearly, use a healer, practitioner or believing friend (as Chrysler's wife believed in him)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the law of agreement\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingTheVisionForAnother (The Game of Life, p. 21): there one asks a friend or healer to see the good when wavering; here the law of agreement is named, and a second person who believes is held needed, as with a wife's faith in her husband."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 13 \"Rivers in the Desert\", p. 230; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWifeBelievedInHim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success through a wife's belief"@en, "Erfolg durch den Glauben der Ehefrau"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most successful men are said to credit their wives' belief; Walter P. Chrysler is quoted on his wife's faith from the first."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 13 \"Rivers in the Desert\", p. 230; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnTalkAboutYourAffairsLittle a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Talking little about one's affairs, and only to encouragers"@en, "Wenig über die eigenen Angelegenheiten reden, und nur mit Ermutigern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Speak of one's affairs as rarely as possible and only to those who give encouragement and inspiration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
