pmc:NewThoughtShinnLeadFromTheExternal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving a lead from the external"@en, "Einen Hinweis von außen erhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "A lead always comes if asked, sometimes as intuition, sometimes from outside: Ada heard a stranger tell another Ada to go, took it as her lead, and it turned out very well."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnMessageOrLead (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 52): there guidance appears in ordinary events; here it comes from outside after a lead has been asked for, in a stranger's remark that names the student."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
