#
# The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSnowWhite a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Snow White read metaphysically; fairy tales founded on Truth"@en, "Schneewittchen metaphysisch gelesen; Märchen in der Wahrheit gegründet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Given on request; fairy tales descend from ancient Persian, Indian and Egyptian legends founded on Truth, which is why adults filled the theatre for Disney's film."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 234; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnInnerMeaningOfSnowWhite a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The author's key to the Snow White tale"@en, "Der Schlüssel der Autorin zu Schneewittchen und den sieben Zwergen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A metaphysical reading of the fairy tale in which each figure stands for a mental factor: Snow White the self, the cruel stepmother a negative thought-form in the subconscious, birds and animals intuitive leads, the dwarfs protective forces, the prince the divine plan."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"Metaphysical interpretation of Snow White\"."@en ;
    skos:note "The single figures of the tale are entered as namings."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Florence Scovel Shinn, in The Secret Door to Success" ;
    dcterms:date "1940"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", pp. 234-237; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCruelStepMother a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The cruel stepmother = a negative thought-form in the subconscious"@en, "Die böse Stiefmutter = eine negative Gedankenform im Unterbewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nearly everyone has one; like all cruel thought-forms it keeps one ragged and out of sight; it is a negative conviction working out in all affairs."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "cruel step-mother; Queen" ;
    pm:nameRole "negative thought-form/conviction in the subconscious" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 234; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFriendlyBirdsAndAnimals a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Friendly birds and animals = intuitive leads or hunches"@en, "Freundliche Vögel und Tiere = intuitive Hinweise oder Ahnungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "They are always ready to get one out of the woods; they tried to give Snow White the hunch not to eat the apple."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "friendly birds and animals" ;
    pm:nameRole "intuitive leads, hunches" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 235; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSevenDwarfs a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Seven Dwarfs = the protective forces about us"@en, "Die sieben Zwerge = die schützenden Kräfte um uns"@de ;
    skos:definition "They come to the rescue, too late when the hunch is ignored."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Seven Dwarfs" ;
    pm:nameRole "protective forces surrounding the person" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 235; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPoisonedApple a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ignoring the hunch not to act (the poisoned apple)"@en, "Die Ahnung ignorieren, nicht zu handeln (der vergiftete Apfel)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Snow White could not resist the apple despite the animals' warning hunch and fell as if dead; the protective forces arrived too late."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnMagicPathOfIntuition fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 236; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnOldThoughtFormDissolved a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Old thought-form dissolved and dissipated forever"@en, "Alte Gedankenform für immer aufgelöst und zerstreut"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the tale's reading, when the divine plan awakens one the old thought-form is gone for good."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 236; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPrinceIsTheDivinePlan a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Prince = one's life's divine plan"@en, "Der Prinz = der göttliche Plan deines Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the divine plan wakes one up one lives happily ever after; the stepmother is swept away."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Prince" ;
    pm:nameRole "the divine plan of one's life" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 236; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnFindYourCruelStepMother a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding the form of tyranny of one's cruel stepmother"@en, "Die Form der Tyrannei der eigenen bösen Stiefmutter finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identify which negative conviction in the subconscious works out in one's affairs (e.g. my good always comes too late), then reverse it with a repeated affirmation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 236; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEternalVigilance a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Eternal vigilance as the cost of freedom from negative thought-forms"@en, "Ewige Wachsamkeit ist der Preis der Freiheit von negativen Gedankenformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must drown out the stepmother's dreary suggestions continually."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnCruelStepMother ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 236; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnLightOfLightsStatement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Closing affirmation: nothing can hinder the Divine Plan; the Light of Lights reveals the Open Road"@en, "Schlussaffirmation: Nichts kann den Göttlichen Plan hindern; das Licht der Lichter enthüllt den Offenen Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "State that nothing can hinder or delay the manifestation of one's Divine Plan and that the Light of Lights shines on one's path revealing the open road to fulfillment."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"The Light of Lights streams on my pathway\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Secret Door to Success (1940), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Three, ch. 14 \"The Inner Meaning of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs\", p. 236; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1940 DeVorss print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWideAwakeToMyGoodYieldsOldThoughtFormDissolved a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Wide-awake affirmation (never missing a trick) yields old thought-form dissolved and dissipated forever"@en, "Affirmation: Ich bin hellwach für mein Gutes, mir entgeht nichts: Alte Gedankenform für immer aufgelöst und zerstreut"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text claims that wide-awake affirmation (never missing a trick) brings about old thought-form dissolved and dissipated forever."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnWideAwakeToMyGood ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnOldThoughtFormDissolved ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnSecretDoorToSuccess ;
